      "path": "VAA.EAPI.Microservices/VAA.EAPI.Microservices.Loyalty.Identity/Application/Command/RegisterUnder18CommandHandler.cs",
      "line": 51,
      "url": "https://github.com/VAAD1ST/eapi/pull/1731#discussion_r3901723935",
      "author": "copilot-pull-request-reviewer",
      "body": "The validation error message hard-codes “U18 dummy email”, but the allowed dummy domain is read from configuration (`DummyEmailDomain`). If the configured domain ever changes, clients will receive a misleading error. Consider making the message domain-agnostic (or include the configured domain) so it stays accurate.",
      "decision": "valid",
      "resolutionComment": "Updated the validation response to say 'system-generated dummy email' without naming the fallback U18 domain. The accepted domain remains configuration-driven through DummyEmailDomain, so the message now stays accurate when that setting changes."
    }
  ],
